# Custom response headers for the Cloudflare Worker's static assets.
# Supported natively by Workers static assets, the same way Pages reads it.
# Copied verbatim into dist/ by Astro; GitHub Pages ignores it.

# The headshots exist to be resized at the edge (/cdn-cgi/image/... — see
# src/lib/cdnImage.ts), and Cloudflare caches a transformed variant only as
# long as the *source* response permits. Workers assets default unhashed files
# to `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which pins every variant to Cloudflare's
# 300s floor and has the transformer re-pulling the original all day (it also
# returns a `cache-control is too restrictive` warning on every transform).
# These sources are 7-10 MB each, so that re-pulling is not cheap.
#
# A week, not a year: these filenames are stable and carry no content hash, so
# replacing someone's photo reuses its URL. A purge makes that immediate; this
# bounds how long a stale copy can linger for anyone who missed the purge.
/images/hod/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
